<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African July M3 money supply grows 14.69 pct.</title>
<headline>S.African July M3 money supply grows 14.69 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's year-on-year broadly defined M3 money supply grew 14.69 percent in July, preliminary Reserve Bank figures show.</p>
<p>June M3 growth was revised to 15.74 percent from a preliminary 15.56 percent.</p>
<p>Annual private sector credit growth was 18.50 percent, preliminary figures showed, against a revised 18.65 percent in June.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast money supply would rise 16.2 percent year-on-year, while private sector credit extension was expected to rise 18.4 percent.  </p>
<p>Detailed data (Percentage changes over 12 months):</p>
<p>July 1996 preliminary M3 growth -- 14.69 percent</p>
<p>July 1996 preliminary private sector credit growth -- 18.50 percent</p>
<p>					   Jun '96		May '96</p>
<p>M3  revised			    15.74		  13.56</p>
<p>M2    &quot;				  17.91		  14.34</p>
<p>M1    &quot;				  28.66		  24.13</p>
<p>Private sector credit growth     18.65		  18.63</p>
<p>Monetary aggregates (Rand millions)</p>
<p>			    Jul '96(prel)  Jun '96 (rev) May '96 (rev)</p>
<p>M3 unadjusted	   302.31	   304.40	  298.14</p>
<p>M3 seasonally adj.    305.87	   306.12	  296.25</p>
<p>Private sector credit 345.79	   341.35	  333.92</p>
<p>M3 annualised growth rate from base of guideline</p>
<p>			     18.22	    21.05	   17.34</p>
<p>(1996 guideline range 6-10 pct)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
